`),sampleAnswer:["Count the atoms in each structure: both contain three carbon atoms, six hydrogen atoms and two oxygen atoms, so both have the molecular formula $\\mathrm{C_3H_6O_2}$.","","However, the atoms are joined to give different functional groups. P ($\\mathrm{CH_3CH_2COOH}$, propanoic acid) has a carboxyl group, $\\mathrm{{-}COOH}$. Q ($\\mathrm{CH_3COOCH_3}$, methyl ethanoate) has an ester group, $\\mathrm{{-}COO{-}}$, linking two carbon groups.","","Same molecular formula plus different functional groups (and so different chemical families) is what defines functional group isomers."].join(`
