`),marks:4}}},mQe=["CH-M8-3"],pQe=["Atom economy in chemical synthesis","Green chemistry principles for industrial processes","Hazard and toxicity of reagents","Evaluating alternative industrial production routes","Addition versus substitution reactions of hydrocarbons"],fQe={id:"chemistry/2024/q31",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...mQe],learningTopics:pQe,generate(t){return{question:["Chloroethane, $\\mathrm{C_2H_5Cl}$, is used as a local anaesthetic spray. A manufacturer is choosing between two ways of making it.","","| Route | Equation | Conditions | Atom economy |","| --- | --- | --- | --- |","| 1 | $\\mathrm{C_2H_4 + HCl \\rightarrow C_2H_5Cl}$ | catalyst, no UV light needed | 100% |","| 2 | $\\mathrm{C_2H_6 + Cl_2 \\rightarrow C_2H_5Cl + HCl}$ | UV light | 63.9% |","","Chlorine gas is very toxic if breathed in. Route 2 also forms some dichloroethane and trichloroethane as side products.","","Recommend one route for the manufacturer. Justify your choice using the information given."].join(`
`),sampleAnswer:["**Recommendation: Route 1** (adding hydrogen chloride to ethene).","","**Atom economy.** Route 1 is an addition reaction: every atom in the reactants ends up in chloroethane, so its atom economy is 100%. Route 2 is a substitution reaction, and the hydrogen chloride it forms is a by-product. Only","$$\\frac{M(\\mathrm{C_2H_5Cl})}{M(\\mathrm{C_2H_6}) + M(\\mathrm{Cl_2})} = \\frac{64.51}{30.07 + 70.90} \\times 100\\% = 63.9\\%$$","of the reactant mass becomes product, so over a third is waste.","","**Hazard.** Route 2 needs chlorine, which is very toxic if inhaled. Storing and handling large amounts of it creates a serious risk to workers and to the surroundings if there is a leak. Route 1 avoids chlorine completely.","","**Yield and purity.** In Route 2 the chlorine can replace more than one hydrogen atom, giving dichloroethane and trichloroethane. These lower the yield of chloroethane and must be separated out. Route 1 gives a single product.","","**Judgement.** Route 1 is better on every point given: less waste, a less hazardous reagent and a purer product. It fits the green chemistry aims of reducing waste and hazard."].join(`
