`)}}}},crt=["DT-DP-10"],hrt=["Market research and target audience analysis","Identifying market trends and consumer preferences","Purchasing power and cost-to-value in consumer decisions","Brand awareness and marketing in design","Sequencing research in the design process"],drt={id:"design_and_technology/2022/q06",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...crt],learningTopics:hrt,generate(t){const e=[0,1,2,3][t],n="Market trends",o=["Brand awareness","Purchasing power","Cost-to-value ratio"],i=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)i.push(s===e?n:o[a++]);return{question:"Which of the following should a designer first consider when conducting an analysis of a targeted audience?",choices:i,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["Market trends should be the first consideration when analysing a targeted audience.","","Understanding current market trends gives the designer an overall picture","of the landscape their product will enter — including what consumers are","currently buying, what is growing in popularity, and what needs are emerging.","This broad context guides all subsequent audience analysis.","","Brand awareness, purchasing power, and cost-to-value ratio are all","important factors to consider, but they are more specific details","that are meaningfully evaluated only after understanding the broader","market environment."].join(`
`)}}}},urt=["DT-DP-12","DT-DP-8"],mrt=["client needs analysis and target market research","user-centred design decision-making","design communication techniques and presentation methods","digital tools for collaboration and feedback in design"],prt={id:"design_and_technology/2022/q07",version:1,variants:4,syllabusTopics:[...urt],learningTopics:mrt,generate(t){const e=[3,0,1,2][t],n="To simulate possible issues that may arise in production",o=["To save time and staff costs","To ensure funding by investors is secured","To demonstrate the final design to the client"],i=[];let a=0;for(let s=0;s<4;s++)i.push(s===e?n:o[a++]);return{question:"Why would a designer make prototypes after creating CAD models for a client?",choices:i,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["A designer makes prototypes after CAD models to simulate possible issues","that may arise in production.","","While CAD models allow the designer to visualise the product digitally,","a physical prototype reveals practical challenges that cannot be detected","on screen — such as structural weaknesses, assembly difficulties, material","behaviour under stress, or ergonomic problems. Identifying these issues","early saves significant time and cost in later production stages.","","Prototyping does not save immediate time or staff costs; it actually","requires additional effort. It is not primarily for securing investor","funding, and it does not represent the final design — the prototype","is a working test model used for refinement."].join(`
