`),_ht={id:"design_and_technology/2025/q13",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...Sht],learningTopics:Cht,generate(t){return{question:["TWO different types of battery power options for a household are shown.",Iht,"Discuss the long-term environmental impact of the battery power options."],sampleAnswer:["Rechargeable lithium ion batteries have a lower long-term environmental impact","compared to disposable alkaline batteries.","","Alkaline batteries are single-use and must be disposed of after each power cycle,","contributing significantly to landfill waste. When improperly disposed of, they","can leach toxic chemicals into soil and waterways.","","Lithium ion batteries can be recharged and reused many times, reducing the volume","of waste produced. However, producing them requires mining finite resources such as","lithium and nickel, which can cause habitat destruction and pollution.","","As consumers become more aware of these impacts, growing demand for responsible","battery recycling programs and sustainable disposal has emerged. Overall,","rechargeable batteries represent the more sustainable long-term option due to","significantly less waste generation."].join(`
`),marks:4}}},qht=["DT-IET-1"],Pht=["Impact of innovation on user experience","Usability and intuitive interface design","Ergonomics in wearable and portable technology","Personalisation and user-centred design","Accessibility improvements through innovation","Case studies of innovative products"],Eht={id:"design_and_technology/2025/q14",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...qht],learningTopics:Pht,generate(t){return{question:"Explain how innovation in design has influenced user experience.",sampleAnswer:["Innovation in design has profoundly transformed user experience by enhancing","functionality, usability, and personalisation across a wide range of products.","","Touch screen technology, for example, replaced physical buttons with intuitive","gesture-based interfaces, making devices such as smartphones dramatically","easier and more natural to use. This lowered the skill barrier for interacting","with technology and enabled a broader range of users to engage with digital devices.","","Wearable technology such as smartwatches and fitness trackers demonstrates how","compact, ergonomic design innovations have integrated technology seamlessly into","everyday life. Users can monitor health metrics, receive notifications, and","interact with connected systems without interrupting their activities.","","Smart home devices — including voice-activated assistants and automated lighting","systems — show how design innovation has created highly personalised experiences.","Users can customise their environments to suit individual preferences and routines,","improving both comfort and convenience.","","Overall, innovation in design has made technology more accessible, efficient,","and tailored to individual needs, significantly improving how users engage with","and benefit from designed products and systems."].join(`
`),marks:6}}},Oht=["DT-IET-3"],Lht=["innovation and emerging technologies in design","social, ethical, and environmental impacts of innovation","extended-response analysis of design issues and impacts"],Nht={id:"design_and_technology/2025/q15",version:1,variants:1,syllabusTopics:[...Oht],learningTopics:Lht,generate(t){return{question:["Recent advancements in artificial intelligence (AI) have transformed the design industry,","influencing how designers create, collaborate, and produce their work. AI tools now assist","in generating design concepts, automating repetitive tasks, and providing insights based","on data analysis.","","Analyse the impact of AI on designers."].join(`
`),sampleAnswer:["Artificial intelligence has had a profound and multifaceted impact on the design industry,","bringing both significant opportunities and important challenges for designers.","","**Efficiency and productivity**","AI tools have dramatically increased the speed at which designers can work.","By automating repetitive tasks such as resizing images, generating colour palettes,","and producing initial layout options, AI frees designers to focus on higher-level","creative decisions. Tools like generative AI can produce multiple design concepts","in seconds, accelerating the ideation phase of the design process.","","**Enhanced creativity and access to information**","AI provides designers with access to a wider variety of design references, styles,","and data-driven insights than would previously have been possible. This can inspire","new directions and support more informed design decisions. People with disabilities","may also benefit, as AI-assisted tools can help create more inclusive design solutions.","","**Ethical concerns**","The use of AI raises significant ethical questions. Intellectual property and copyright","issues arise when AI generates designs trained on existing designers' work without","proper attribution or compensation. Bias in AI training data can lead to designs","that reflect and perpetuate existing inequalities. Privacy concerns emerge when AI","systems collect and analyse user data to personalise design outputs.","","**Automation and job displacement**","There is growing concern that AI may displace design jobs, particularly for entry-level","roles involving routine tasks. As AI takes over more technical work, the skills valued","in designers may shift from execution to conceptual thinking and creative direction.","This creates a risk of a digital divide — between designers who can effectively use AI","tools and those who cannot access or afford them.","","**Dependency and loss of creativity**","Heavy reliance on AI tools risks reducing designers' own creative development.","If designers consistently accept AI-generated outputs rather than developing their","own ideas, this may lead to a homogenisation of design styles and a loss of the","human connection that gives design cultural and emotional resonance.","","**Conclusion**","The impact of AI on designers is transformative but complex. While AI offers powerful","tools that improve efficiency and expand creative possibilities, it also introduces","ethical, social, and professional challenges. Designers who critically evaluate and","thoughtfully integrate AI into their practice — rather than becoming entirely dependent","on it — are best positioned to harness its benefits while maintaining their creative","identity and professional relevance."].join(`
`),marks:15}}},Mht=[Wct,Gct,Kct,Zct,nht,aht,lht,uht,ght,bht],Rht=[xht,Aht,_ht,Eht,Nht],jht={2015:{multipleChoicesGenerators:stt,writingGenerators:rtt},2016:{multipleChoicesGenerators:nnt,writingGenerators:ont},2017:{multipleChoicesGenerators:not,writingGenerators:oot},2018:{multipleChoicesGenerators:oit,writingGenerators:iit},2019:{multipleChoicesGenerators:Jit,writingGenerators:Zit},2020:{multipleChoicesGenerators:Wat,writingGenerators:Yat},2021:{multipleChoicesGenerators:Bst,writingGenerators:Dst},2022:{multipleChoicesGenerators:Yrt,writingGenerators:Urt},2023:{multipleChoicesGenerators:Wlt,writingGenerators:Ylt},2024:{multipleChoicesGenerators:Hct,writingGenerators:Bct},2025:{multipleChoicesGenerators:Mht,writingGenerators:Rht}};function Fht(t,e,n){return[["Center Number:","","⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚","","Student Number:","","⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚ ⬚","","**HIGHER SCHOOL CERTIFICATE (HSC) EXAMINATION**"].join(`
