`)],choices:n,sampleAnswer:{correctChoiceIndex:e,explanation:["The photoelectric equation is:","","$$E_{k,\\max} = hf - W$$","","where $W$ is the work function of the metal.","","The **slope** of the $E_{k,\\max}$ vs $f$ graph equals $h$ (Planck's constant),","which does not change.","","The **y-intercept** equals $-W$ (the negative work function). A lower line","(Line Y) means a more negative intercept, i.e., a **larger work function**.","","Therefore, Line Y is obtained by using a metal with a **greater work function**.","","Note: Intensity does not affect maximum KE; it only affects the number of","photoelectrons emitted per second."].join(`
