`),sampleAnswer:["**Feature 1: Laminated iron core**","","The iron core is made of thin sheets (laminations) insulated from each other.","This breaks up the conducting paths within the core, reducing the magnitude","of **eddy currents** induced by the changing magnetic flux.","Smaller eddy currents mean less energy is dissipated as heat ($P = I^2R$),","increasing efficiency.","","**Feature 2: Copper wire windings**","","Copper has very low electrical resistivity. Using copper wire minimises the","resistance $R$ of the coil windings.","This reduces the power lost as heat in the coils ($P = I^2R$),","so more of the input power is transferred to the output, increasing efficiency.","","*(Alternative — Continuous iron core:*","*A closed-loop iron core concentrates and confines the magnetic flux,*","*minimising flux leakage. This ensures that nearly all the magnetic field*","*produced by the primary passes through the secondary, maximising flux linkage*","*and therefore efficiency.)*"].join(`
