`),parts:[{question:"Starting from Newton's law of universal gravitation, derive this relationship.",sampleAnswer:["In a circular orbit, gravity is the only force on the orbiting body, so it","supplies all of the centripetal force:","$$\\frac{mv^2}{r} = \\frac{GMm}{r^2}$$","","The body travels one circumference in one period, so $v = \\dfrac{2\\pi r}{T}$.","Substituting:","$$\\frac{m}{r}\\left(\\frac{2\\pi r}{T}\\right)^2 = \\frac{GMm}{r^2}$$","$$\\frac{4\\pi^2 r}{T^2} = \\frac{GM}{r^2}$$","Multiplying both sides by $r^2$ and dividing by $4\\pi^2$:","$$\\frac{r^3}{T^2} = \\frac{GM}{4\\pi^2}$$","","The mass $m$ of the orbiting body cancels, so the relationship is the same","for every body orbiting the same central mass."].join(`
